{"kind":"article","sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The benchmark suite measures the same workloads at several committed FirebladeECS revisions, such as a release tag against "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"main"},{"type":"text","text":". The workloads cover entity creation, destruction and lookup, adding and removing components, iterating families, system updates and component events. Revisions with value-type components run each workload on both the "},{"code":"archetype","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the "},{"code":"sparseSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" storage (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"), so a report also shows what the storage choice costs."}]},{"level":3,"text":"How results are made trustworthy","type":"heading","anchor":"How-results-are-made-trustworthy"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each revision is built once and measured in "},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" independent process replicates, interleaved in a seeded random order. The replicate is the unit of analysis: the centre value is the median of the replicate medians, with a distribution-free order-statistic 95% confidence interval. A speed-up against the baseline is the Hodges–Lehmann estimate with its exact confidence interval, tested with an exact Mann–Whitney test and adjusted across all comparisons of a report with Benjamini–Hochberg. A change counts as "},{"code":"faster","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"slower","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" only when it is significant and clears the ±5% equivalence zone; an interval inside that zone is reported as "},{"code":"equivalent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", anything else as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inconclusive"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Read and reproduce","anchor":"Read-and-reproduce"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The latest published report: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/"},{"type":"text","text":". Reports are published for dedicated benchmark releases only; the page shows the newest."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The 2.0.0 report: "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/fireblade-engine.github.io\/ecs\/benchmarks\/2.0.0\/","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", the full suite with 10 replicates on both storages. Its source is committed as "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/fireblade-engine\/ecs\/blob\/main\/Documentation\/Benchmarks\/BenchmarkReport.html","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The statistical design and workload parity notes: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/fireblade-engine\/ecs\/blob\/main\/Documentation\/Benchmarks\/Methodology.md"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To measure revisions locally, pass comma-separated tags, branches or commit IDs. Results are saved under "},{"code":"Benchmarks\/Results\/<UTC timestamp>\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing","code":["make benchmark-compare REFS=1.4.3,main:2.0.0 REPLICATES=10 BENCHMARK_FILTER='.*'","make benchmark-report RESULTS=\"Benchmarks\/Results\/<run>\/*.json\" REPORT_BASELINE=1.4.3"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BENCHMARK_FILTER"},{"type":"text","text":" only 16 entities of every workload plus "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entity.create.no-entities"},{"type":"text","text":" (which only has 0 entities) run. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"make benchmark-report"},{"type":"text","text":" renders the single file "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BenchmarkReport.html"},{"type":"text","text":" from saved results and never runs benchmarks. See "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Benchmarks\/README.md"},{"type":"text","text":" for all options."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"See how FirebladeECS revisions compare on a shared workload suite, and run the comparison yourself."}],"metadata":{"title":"Benchmarks","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/benchmarks"]}],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn the API and key types Fireblade provides to compose your game or app logic."}],"title":"Getting started with Fireblade ECS","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/gettingstartedwithfirebladeecs","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and know what changes."}],"title":"Choosing a storage","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage","role":"article"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventDelegate":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A delegate for receiving Nexus events and errors."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventDelegate"}],"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventdelegate","title":"NexusEventDelegate","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventDelegate"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ComponentMacro":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Implement registration, cloning, snapshots and inspection for a component from its stored properties.","type":"text"}],"title":"Generating components with